    "previous_model_response": "Since \\(O\\) is the center, \\(OA=OB=OC\\).\n\n- In \\(\\triangle AOB\\), \\(OA=OB\\), so \\(\\angle BAO=\\angle ABO=30^\\circ\\). Thus  \n  \\[\n  \\angle AOB=180^\\circ-30^\\circ-30^\\circ=120^\\circ.\n  \\]\n\n- In \\(\\triangle AOC\\), \\(OA=OC\\), so \\(\\angle OAC=\\angle ACO=40^\\circ\\). Thus  \n  \\[\n  \\angle AOC=180^\\circ-40^\\circ-40^\\circ=100^\\circ.\n  \\]\n\nAngles around \\(O\\) sum to \\(360^\\circ\\), hence\n\\[\n\\angle BOC=360^\\circ-120^\\circ-100^\\circ=140^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nD",
